      "worked": "The longer diagonal forms a triangle with sides 12 cm, 18 cm and 22 cm. Its angle $\\theta$ opposite the diagonal is the obtuse angle of the parallelogram.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}22^2&=12^2+18^2-2\\times12\\times18\\cos\\theta\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{12^2+18^2-22^2}{2\\times12\\times18}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-\\frac{1}{27}\\\\\\theta&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{1}{27}\\right)\\\\\\theta&\\approx92.1^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
